# How to fence node "node-a" (used by its peer when node-a must be shot).
# The file name MUST match the DRBD node name (the `on <name> { ... }` in the
# resource / what DRBD reports as the peer). Mode 0600 -- it holds credentials.
#
# IPMI via fence_ipmilan. 'ip' is the BMC address, not the node's OS address.
AGENT=/usr/sbin/fence_ipmilan
ip=10.0.0.1
lanplus=1
login=admin
password=CHANGEME
method=onoff
# No 'delay=' here: the handler computes the priority-fencing-delay itself
# (Primary-majority node fences first). See FENCE_DELAY in fence.conf.
